A HDD was secured onto the middle console to the left of the driver, the standard location for vehicles in the United Kingdom. Only one display was used at a time to ensure that the participant knew where to look for task information.
The size and color of visual stimuli as presented via both displays were visually matched to appear as close as possible. Participants’ eye gazes were recorded using an SMI eye tracking system with BeGaze analysis software,

