There was no difference in the SDLP for HUD and HDD for either the text (Z-score = 1.034, p-value = 0.301) or grid tasks (Z-score = 1.138, p-value = 0.255). Therefore, the HUD did not have a significant effect on driving performance.

Response Time As expected, secondary task response times were not normally distributed, nor was the commonly used log transform of response times (although it nearly met the criteria). As such, we used the Wilcoxon Signed Rank test and observed no significant differences between response times across the two display types in the grid visual search task condition (p=0.081, Z=1.396). We did however see a significant difference between the HUD and HDD in the text visual search condition (p=0.002, Z=2.947). This suggests an interaction effect between the display type (HUD or HDD) and image (Grid or Text) presented to the user (Figure 8).

