Display Preference Overall, participants preferred head up displays for both the text (78%) and grid visual search tasks (80%). However, the legibility of the HDD-text display was preferred over the HUD-text display (63%). This is congruent with Kerr’s findings in a study considering AR personal navigation devices where participants reported that they were unable to effectively read text in HUDs, but that they generally liked using the AR devices [10]. Another possible explanation for the lack of legibility in the HUD is the inherent interaction between HUD text and driving scene backgrounds as observed by Gabbard, Swan & Hix [14] as well as Gattullo et al. [15].

